{"id":"anti-example-001","type":"pattern","fact":"Example: NEVER use 'as any' type casting - it hides bugs and defeats TypeScript's type system.","recommendation":"Use proper type narrowing, generics, or 'as unknown as Type' for test mocks.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"documentation","reference":"TypeScript patterns guide","date":"2026-01-09"}],"tags":["typescript","type-safety"],"affectedFiles":["**/*.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id": "antipattern-test-fake-diverges-from-real-handle-001", "type": "pattern", "fact": "A test fake that diverges from the real handle's behavior masks production bugs. In #79 the SignalFlowSpec recording fake captured _ch_sendChunk, but the REAL Signal/Telegram ChannelHandle no-ops _ch_sendChunk (they don't stream) — so tests were green while production provider output was discarded entirely.", "recommendation": "Make fakes mirror the real handle's per-method behavior, especially which methods are no-ops. When a Handle has both a streaming and a whole-message path, the fake for a non-streaming channel must no-op the streaming method just like production, or assert on the path the real channel actually uses.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "feat/tabs-as-view-refactor (#79) WU8 cutover close-out + 8d.g adversarial review", "date": "2026-06-11"}], "tags": ["testing", "fakes", "mocks", "channel", "gotcha"], "affectedFiles": ["test/Integration/SignalFlowSpec.hs"], "affectedServices": ["ChannelHandle"], "createdAt": "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
{"id": "antipattern-silent-drop-seams-001", "type": "pattern", "fact": "Silent-drop seams violate PureClaw's everything-visible principle. The #79 cutover introduced several: discarding the Either TabError from sendTo (input lost when a tab's queue is full), swallowing the provider stream exception with no message, and ignoring StreamWarning. Each silently dropped user-facing signal.", "recommendation": "Never discard an Either/error from a delivery seam or swallow a provider exception without surfacing it. On Left, emit a banner; on stream failure, surface a visible error event; log warnings. Audit `_ <- action` and bare exception catches on any user-facing path.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "feat/tabs-as-view-refactor (#79) WU8 cutover close-out + 8d.g adversarial review", "date": "2026-06-11"}], "tags": ["everything-visible", "error-handling", "ux", "tabs"], "affectedFiles": ["src/PureClaw/Routing/TabDispatch.hs", "src/PureClaw/Agent/Turn.hs"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-06-11T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
